@* Replaces Users.ascx + Users.ascx.cs + Users.ascx.designer.cs.

   Users.ascx was a single @@ Control directive with no markup at all, and both the code-behind and
   the designer file declared an empty class body: the control exists purely as the host that the
   user-accounts page loads so that the UserUserControlBase event surface (UserCreated,
   UserDeleted, UserRestored, UserRemoved, UserUpdated and their error events) is available to the
   page that wires it up. There is therefore nothing to render and nothing to port beyond the base
   class, which is already the Blazor UserUserControlBase.

   The unused `using` list the code-behind carried (System.Web.UI, System.Web.UI.WebControls,
   System.Web.UI.HtmlControls, ClientResourceManagement, ...) referenced no symbol in the empty
   body and is not reproduced. *@

@namespace DotNetNuke.Modules.Admin.Users
@inherits DotNetNuke.Entities.Modules.UserUserControlBase
